      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to District of Columbia?",
      "a": "The District of Columbia has $22B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The District recorded 33,933 awards with an average award size of $649K, and obligations fell down 30.0% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows $31B in FY21, $31.6B in FY22, $33.9B in FY23, $36B in FY24, and $31.4B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in District of Columbia?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense, the Department of Transportation, and the General Services Administration award the most contracts in the District of Columbia. The Department of Defense obligated $4.2B, the Department of Transportation obligated $3B, and the General Services Administration obligated $2.9B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $2.5B and the Department of State obligated $1.3B."
